   "summary": "Wang Fang of Quenvara Energy Technology (Huizhou), supplier SUP-0011 (active, Net 30, on file, stated link plus an inferred legacy record V10560), sent quotation QV-Q-2609-17 on 2026-09-21 for 2027 battery packs. It is the only message in its thread and corrects nothing. Offers: HR-50110 Tern pack (QV-48L30-HR) USD 1,155.21 each from Huizhou or USD 1,224.52 from a new Penang, Malaysia plant; HR-50210 Porter pack (QV-48L60-HR) USD 2,111.81 from Huizhou or USD 2,238.52 from Penang. Validity runs to 2026-11-05 (45 days), FOB Shenzhen or FOB Penang. Penang lead time is 60 days, available from February 2027 after qualification (UN38.3 and UL 2271 reports need updating). Penang packs use Huizhou cells, so origin is for the customs broker to rule and must not be assumed from the assembly site; a duty comparison needs that ruling before the Penang option is chosen. Priya Nair should decide before 2026-11-05 and confirm the origin question with the broker.",
